(713638, 76117, 1009, '<td valign="top">This is a great picture. With a little work I think you could have a winner! As it is I feel the light blow out on the flowers to be just a little to much. Great pic though!!!</td>', 'This is a great picture. With a little work I think you could have a winner! As it is I feel the light blow out on the flowers to be just a little to much. Great pic though!!!', '2004-05-12 08:22:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(713640, 74764, 20685, '<td valign="top">nice idea, but out of focus</td>', 'nice idea, but out of focus', '2004-05-12 08:23:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(713642, 75572, 9295, '<td valign="top">If the lack of focus is intentional, it doesn''t work at all, I''m afraid. Also, I think the idea of using a chess game to illustrate opposites is a good idea, but it might be more effective if the pieces were the more traditional black &amp; white kind to bring the point home. The similar colors of the pieces and the shadows don''t illustrate the theme as well as if there were more stark contrast.</td>', 'If the lack of focus is intentional, it doesn''t work at all, I''m afraid. Also, I think the idea of using a chess game to illustrate opposites is a good idea, but it might be more effective if the pieces were the more traditional black & white kind to bring the point home. The similar colors of the pieces and the shadows don''t illustrate the theme as well as if there were more stark contrast.', '2004-05-12 08:26:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(713643, 76060, 20685, '<td valign="top">lovely, simple and clever - love the hue too - 10 from me</td>', 'lovely, simple and clever - love the hue too - 10 from me', '2004-05-12 08:28:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(713644, 75548, 9295, '<td valign="top">Ooh, I like this a lot except that the black kitty gets lost against the dark background. Is there anything that can be done with lighting to bring him out a little more?  Otherwise, I love the way they are "posed", particularly the white cat and they''re eyes being the only color in the shot is neat since (I assume) this is a natural phenomenon and not a trick of post processing.</td>', 'Ooh, I like this a lot except that the black kitty gets lost against the dark background. Is there anything that can be done with lighting to bring him out a little more?  Otherwise, I love the way they are "posed", particularly the white cat and they''re eyes being the only color in the shot is neat since (I assume) this is a natural phenomenon and not a trick of post processing.', '2004-05-12 08:31:29.000000', NULL, 1),
