(717873, 75704, 6388, '<td valign="top">Wouldn''t that be mare and foal? ;)  As for the picture, the colour seems a little washed out to me.  I shoot horses a lot, and I find you need to really boost the contrast (I use curves to do it) or it looks flat.  Another habit of mine is to try not to cut off a horse in the midsection...I''d move the crop a little in either direction; either use a leg as a frame, or completely include or exclude them.  I doubt that''s an official photography rule, it''s just one of mine.  I like the fact that it looks as if they''re hugging.  Nice moment you caught here.</td>', 'Wouldn''t that be mare and foal? ;)  As for the picture, the colour seems a little washed out to me.  I shoot horses a lot, and I find you need to really boost the contrast (I use curves to do it) or it looks flat.  Another habit of mine is to try not to cut off a horse in the midsection...I''d move the crop a little in either direction; either use a leg as a frame, or completely include or exclude them.  I doubt that''s an official photography rule, it''s just one of mine.  I like the fact that it looks as if they''re hugging.  Nice moment you caught here.', '2004-05-14 04:14:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(717878, 75063, 18080, '<td valign="top">Nice idea.<br/>Looks like it was taken with disposable one</td>', 'Nice idea.Looks like it was taken with disposable one', '2004-05-14 04:49:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(717888, 75670, 6130, '<td valign="top">Funny and very good and I love it.10</td>', 'Funny and very good and I love it.10', '2004-05-14 05:49:10.000000', NULL, 1),
