(718893, 75063, 20539, '<td valign="top">good idea. the title would be better if the 2 zeros werent there. then its really just going from 3.99 to 399. nice shot anyway -7</td>', 'good idea. the title would be better if the 2 zeros werent there. then its really just going from 3.99 to 399. nice shot anyway -7', '2004-05-14 18:17:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(718894, 75920, 20539, '<td valign="top">very mesmorizing shot. great title for it too! - 9</td>', 'very mesmorizing shot. great title for it too! - 9', '2004-05-14 18:18:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(718897, 75742, 19780, '<td valign="top">Great colors and composition. The placement of the figure is a bit of an optical illusion because of the shadow. I don''t get the sense of opposition since there''s really nothing solid portrayed. Very inventive entry.</td>', 'Great colors and composition. The placement of the figure is a bit of an optical illusion because of the shadow. I don''t get the sense of opposition since there''s really nothing solid portrayed. Very inventive entry.', '2004-05-14 18:18:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(718898, 76110, 20539, '<td valign="top">light reflexions are too strong. a different light source would have been better</td>', 'light reflexions are too strong. a different light source would have been better', '2004-05-14 18:19:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(718900, 75717, 19780, '<td valign="top">A wonderfully simple photo. Your exposre is good, though I might like to see the candle placed slightly off center to give the darkness more dominance to underscore the opposition.</td>', 'A wonderfully simple photo. Your exposre is good, though I might like to see the candle placed slightly off center to give the darkness more dominance to underscore the opposition.', '2004-05-14 18:19:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(718902, 75952, 21761, '<td valign="top">Excellent attention to detail.  I like how you''ve oriented both the map and the compass toward magnetic north.  I also like your greyscale - you''ve used the entire range available to you and provide good visual contrast.  I''m not sure you captured the "opposite" theme, however.  Am I missing the point?  A map and compass by design "go together" - they are not opposites.  Perhaps a different challenge.</td>', 'Excellent attention to detail.  I like how you''ve oriented both the map and the compass toward magnetic north.  I also like your greyscale - you''ve used the entire range available to you and provide good visual contrast.  I''m not sure you captured the "opposite" theme, however.  Am I missing the point?  A map and compass by design "go together" - they are not opposites.  Perhaps a different challenge.', '2004-05-14 18:21:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(718906, 76019, 21761, '<td valign="top">Nice work - I''m getting heartburn just looking at it.  Color seems a bit off though (a little too much red?).</td>', 'Nice work - I''m getting heartburn just looking at it.  Color seems a bit off though (a little too much red?).', '2004-05-14 18:24:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(718908, 75844, 21761, '<td valign="top">Short vs. tall - that''s an opposite.  Still growing?  I''m not sure how that''s fits the challenge.  Otherwise, a very nice greyscale.</td>', 'Short vs. tall - that''s an opposite.  Still growing?  I''m not sure how that''s fits the challenge.  Otherwise, a very nice greyscale.', '2004-05-14 18:25:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(718910, 75251, 21761, '<td valign="top">Too dark - the clouds in the background are brighter than your bright "stone," so your opposite objects don''t seem to contrast enough.</td>', 'Too dark - the clouds in the background are brighter than your bright "stone," so your opposite objects don''t seem to contrast enough.', '2004-05-14 18:27:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(718911, 75280, 21761, '<td valign="top">No comment.</td>', 'No comment.', '2004-05-14 18:29:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(718914, 76071, 21761, '<td valign="top">Your title and subjects agree with each other - so you''ve definitely captured the "opposite" concept.  Over-zealous use of the sharpening filter, however.  Also, if spider is moving from right to left, then it should have been framed right-of-center.</td>', 'Your title and subjects agree with each other - so you''ve definitely captured the "opposite" concept.  Over-zealous use of the sharpening filter, however.  Also, if spider is moving from right to left, then it should have been framed right-of-center.', '2004-05-14 18:33:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(718917, 76020, 21761, '<td valign="top">Nice reflection.  Yet, is a mirror image truly an opposite?</td>', 'Nice reflection.  Yet, is a mirror image truly an opposite?', '2004-05-14 18:35:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(718919, 75601, 21761, '<td valign="top">Opposite sex, indeed.  But the image as a whole doesn''t convey "opposite."  Otherwise, good detail and frame.</td>', 'Opposite sex, indeed.  But the image as a whole doesn''t convey "opposite."  Otherwise, good detail and frame.', '2004-05-14 18:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(718922, 76010, 21761, '<td valign="top">Not quite.  If the Gbelt had a warm or hot hue AND had the ice bucket been sweating (i.e., filled with cold ice in a hot room), then you might have captured the concept.  Otherwise, a warm bucket and a cool-colored gbelt doesn''t get there.</td>', 'Not quite.  If the Gbelt had a warm or hot hue AND had the ice bucket been sweating (i.e., filled with cold ice in a hot room), then you might have captured the concept.  Otherwise, a warm bucket and a cool-colored gbelt doesn''t get there.', '2004-05-14 18:41:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(718927, 75834, 21761, '<td valign="top">No comment.</td>', 'No comment.', '2004-05-14 18:43:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(718929, 75816, 21761, '<td valign="top">Beautiful detail and frame.  Young small green leaves vs. old large brown leaf.  You captured "opposite" and all of your visual cues support each other.  I like your figure vs. ground, too.</td>', 'Beautiful detail and frame.  Young small green leaves vs. old large brown leaf.  You captured "opposite" and all of your visual cues support each other.  I like your figure vs. ground, too.', '2004-05-14 18:46:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(718930, 76044, 21761, '<td valign="top">No comment.</td>', 'No comment.', '2004-05-14 18:47:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(718932, 74994, 21761, '<td valign="top">Nice concept, but inefficient use of negative space.  Also, the pennies (as a set) appear slightly left-of-center.</td>', 'Nice concept, but inefficient use of negative space.  Also, the pennies (as a set) appear slightly left-of-center.', '2004-05-14 18:48:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(718936, 76088, 21761, '<td valign="top">So which do you drink?  Background is, perhaps, too light - which doesn''t allow your objects to consume the entire grey scale.  The words "Coca Cola" are white on a can, but appear neutral grey in your image.  You definitely captured "opposite" though.</td>', 'So which do you drink?  Background is, perhaps, too light - which doesn''t allow your objects to consume the entire grey scale.  The words "Coca Cola" are white on a can, but appear neutral grey in your image.  You definitely captured "opposite" though.', '2004-05-14 18:51:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(718937, 75321, 20822, '<td valign="top">Nicer idea than most. Interesting that you choose to have cups and spoons touch the other side.</td>', 'Nicer idea than most. Interesting that you choose to have cups and spoons touch the other side.', '2004-05-14 18:53:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(718938, 74661, 20822, '<td valign="top">Like my own entry I think you missed the theme.</td>', 'Like my own entry I think you missed the theme.', '2004-05-14 18:54:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(718939, 75280, 19780, '<td valign="top">A very interesting set up for this challenge. I like the forced perspective, showing that it is point of view that allows one to judge something as a positive or negative. I would have liked to see a little higher contrast to this shot. Very well done.</td>', 'A very interesting set up for this challenge. I like the forced perspective, showing that it is point of view that allows one to judge something as a positive or negative. I would have liked to see a little higher contrast to this shot. Very well done.', '2004-05-14 18:56:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(718941, 76009, 20822, '<td valign="top">I can''t wait to see where this is. I am always amazed at "if you build it someone will buy it"<br/>Good idea and composition</td>', 'I can''t wait to see where this is. I am always amazed at "if you build it someone will buy it"Good idea and composition', '2004-05-14 18:57:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(718942, 75706, 19780, '<td valign="top">An interesting take - a large dog, a small dog, a curly haired dog, a straight haired dog, a white dog, a black dog. I might have liked to see the black dog more in frame or the white dog cropped out a little more. Nice balance - the background of a neutral red helps.</td>', 'An interesting take - a large dog, a small dog, a curly haired dog, a straight haired dog, a white dog, a black dog. I might have liked to see the black dog more in frame or the white dog cropped out a little more. Nice balance - the background of a neutral red helps.', '2004-05-14 18:58:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(718944, 76020, 20822, '<td valign="top">I like the photo. The title suggests differing view points which I don''t see. Rated the photo a 6</td>', 'I like the photo. The title suggests differing view points which I don''t see. Rated the photo a 6', '2004-05-14 18:59:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(718947, 76107, 20822, '<td valign="top">The photo is a little fuzzy. Would another angle have eliminated the glare?</td>', 'The photo is a little fuzzy. Would another angle have eliminated the glare?', '2004-05-14 19:01:56.000000', NULL, 1),
