(719890, 74604, 21761, '<td valign="top">I think your title helped me - otherwise I would have thought "different" and not "opposite."  I like how your figure has focus and your ground does not, but I think the flowers (at bottom) provide too much contrast -- they don''t seem to stay in the background despite the lack of focus.  Perhaps others will disagree, but I think the flowers (at bottom) are competing with your lemons for attention.</td>', 'I think your title helped me - otherwise I would have thought "different" and not "opposite."  I like how your figure has focus and your ground does not, but I think the flowers (at bottom) provide too much contrast -- they don''t seem to stay in the background despite the lack of focus.  Perhaps others will disagree, but I think the flowers (at bottom) are competing with your lemons for attention.', '2004-05-15 14:21:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(719892, 75968, 12252, '<td valign="top">Meets the challenge but you cut off the points top and bottom when you cropped, and the white shape is a smidgeon too far to the left near the bottom.</td>', 'Meets the challenge but you cut off the points top and bottom when you cropped, and the white shape is a smidgeon too far to the left near the bottom.', '2004-05-15 14:23:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(719894, 75993, 21313, '<td valign="top">This is a cute picture, but I don''t see how it''s opposites.</td>', 'This is a cute picture, but I don''t see how it''s opposites.', '2004-05-15 14:25:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(719897, 75985, 21761, '<td valign="top">Nicely done - your title helps.  The new international-style glass structure and the old (gothic? romanesque?) building do provide an intersting contrast. Silly architect. The image seems a bit dark - the brightest objects are the clouds, which, in my opinion, don''t stay in the background where they belong.</td>', 'Nicely done - your title helps.  The new international-style glass structure and the old (gothic? romanesque?) building do provide an intersting contrast. Silly architect. The image seems a bit dark - the brightest objects are the clouds, which, in my opinion, don''t stay in the background where they belong.', '2004-05-15 14:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(719899, 75321, 18757, '<td valign="top">wawww. This is cute.I like this.</td>', 'wawww. This is cute.I like this.', '2004-05-15 14:27:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(719901, 75954, 21313, '<td valign="top">I like the picture, but it''s hard to tell how it''s opposites.</td>', 'I like the picture, but it''s hard to tell how it''s opposites.', '2004-05-15 14:28:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(719906, 75903, 21761, '<td valign="top">Wow - great photo.  Your colors and tones really help differentiate your two objects (cool colored chalk and warm colored cheese).  Neutral background texture is nice too.  Perhaps I''m missing the point, but how are chalk and cheese opposites of one another?  Perhaps edible vs. inedible?</td>', 'Wow - great photo.  Your colors and tones really help differentiate your two objects (cool colored chalk and warm colored cheese).  Neutral background texture is nice too.  Perhaps I''m missing the point, but how are chalk and cheese opposites of one another?  Perhaps edible vs. inedible?', '2004-05-15 14:32:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(719910, 74744, 18757, '<td valign="top">super...</td>', 'super...', '2004-05-15 14:35:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(719912, 75184, 21313, '<td valign="top">I like the black and white sheep... it would have been nice since they are black and white to have the picture in color.</td>', 'I like the black and white sheep... it would have been nice since they are black and white to have the picture in color.', '2004-05-15 14:35:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(719913, 75774, 21761, '<td valign="top">Indeed, black and white are opposites, but your objects are not.  As your title indicates, all are different kinds of the same thing: a game.  So, I think there''s a mismatch between visual cues - the differences in tone (black vs. white) and the variations of game don''t support each other.</td>', 'Indeed, black and white are opposites, but your objects are not.  As your title indicates, all are different kinds of the same thing: a game.  So, I think there''s a mismatch between visual cues - the differences in tone (black vs. white) and the variations of game don''t support each other.', '2004-05-15 14:36:35.000000', NULL, 1),
