(721160, 76010, 8624, '<td valign="top">clever interpretation of the challenge. I think you could have brought out "hot" a little more with some additional props in the background (a discarded shoe or piece of clothing) but the rumpled sheets do a good job.</td>', 'clever interpretation of the challenge. I think you could have brought out "hot" a little more with some additional props in the background (a discarded shoe or piece of clothing) but the rumpled sheets do a good job.', '2004-05-16 13:17:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(721161, 74599, 8624, '<td valign="top">clever use of subject material. really no excuse for being so out of focus though.</td>', 'clever use of subject material. really no excuse for being so out of focus though.', '2004-05-16 13:18:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(721165, 75262, 11769, '<td valign="top">You should look at my site and see the photo for  Where You Live Challenge. Same Bridge. Picture is slightly downsloping to the right. Otherwisse nice shot.</td>', 'You should look at my site and see the photo for  Where You Live Challenge. Same Bridge. Picture is slightly downsloping to the right. Otherwisse nice shot.', '2004-05-16 13:20:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(721166, 76093, 8624, '<td valign="top">the lighting looks a bit strange here with a harsh shadow under the pump and no shadow at all under the hiking boot. also the lighting is very flat and the tonal ranges rather narrow. The blacks in the image should be deeper and richer to bring out the textures in your subjects.</td>', 'the lighting looks a bit strange here with a harsh shadow under the pump and no shadow at all under the hiking boot. also the lighting is very flat and the tonal ranges rather narrow. The blacks in the image should be deeper and richer to bring out the textures in your subjects.', '2004-05-16 13:22:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(721176, 75805, 21761, '<td valign="top">Interesting instance of Yin Yang, so I think you captured an "opposite."  Framed well, good figure/ground relationship, but that thing in the background (UL corner) is a bit distracting.  Also, the black dog''s head lacks detail and seems unclear - probably because it was moving.</td>', 'Interesting instance of Yin Yang, so I think you captured an "opposite."  Framed well, good figure/ground relationship, but that thing in the background (UL corner) is a bit distracting.  Also, the black dog''s head lacks detail and seems unclear - probably because it was moving.', '2004-05-16 13:33:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(721177, 75913, 21761, '<td valign="top">Great clarity and detail.  Black &amp; white contrast well (obviously).  But, what I really like is how your board and the underlying wood table share the same yellow hue - which allows both to coexist in the background.  Nice work.</td>', 'Great clarity and detail.  Black & white contrast well (obviously).  But, what I really like is how your board and the underlying wood table share the same yellow hue - which allows both to coexist in the background.  Nice work.', '2004-05-16 13:37:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(721179, 76033, 21761, '<td valign="top">Intersting variation on a common theme.  Seems to lack clarity and focus.  Also, but for your title, I may not have known immediately that the objects surrounding the candle were ice chunks.  The layout works well.</td>', 'Intersting variation on a common theme.  Seems to lack clarity and focus.  Also, but for your title, I may not have known immediately that the objects surrounding the candle were ice chunks.  The layout works well.', '2004-05-16 13:42:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(721185, 75815, 21761, '<td valign="top">Nice work.  Very interesting play on up-side-down vs. right-side-up - it works in several ways (horizontally and vertically).  Focus and clarity are good.  All of the individual parts seem great, but as a whole the image lacks some umph.  (Sorry - I cannot find the right word.)</td>', 'Nice work.  Very interesting play on up-side-down vs. right-side-up - it works in several ways (horizontally and vertically).  Focus and clarity are good.  All of the individual parts seem great, but as a whole the image lacks some umph.  (Sorry - I cannot find the right word.)', '2004-05-16 13:49:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(721187, 74748, 21761, '<td valign="top">Wow, stunning clarity in the immediate foreground.  Great color, interesting detail and nice layout.  The image might have captured "opposite" more concisely had the flower in the mid-ground not been present.  Rather than two layers (figure and ground / focus and unfocused), I cannot help but see three layers -- that right-most flower.  So, ultimately, I think you captured a gradient of focus and not two stark opposites.</td>', 'Wow, stunning clarity in the immediate foreground.  Great color, interesting detail and nice layout.  The image might have captured "opposite" more concisely had the flower in the mid-ground not been present.  Rather than two layers (figure and ground / focus and unfocused), I cannot help but see three layers -- that right-most flower.  So, ultimately, I think you captured a gradient of focus and not two stark opposites.', '2004-05-16 13:57:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(721189, 76078, 10818, '<td valign="top">Well done, nice photo.  Great idea.</td>', 'Well done, nice photo.  Great idea.', '2004-05-16 14:11:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(721191, 75749, 10818, '<td valign="top">I love the sparks, great photo.</td>', 'I love the sparks, great photo.', '2004-05-16 14:11:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(721194, 75683, 10818, '<td valign="top">Being an Astro''s fan, Cubs lose sounds good to me.  :)<br/>Should be a tight race all year.<br/>Funny photo, very original idea, nice job.</td>', 'Being an Astro''s fan, Cubs lose sounds good to me.  :)Should be a tight race all year.Funny photo, very original idea, nice job.', '2004-05-16 14:17:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(721198, 75104, 19841, '<td valign="top">Um, I hate to be the one to break this to you, but steel is not the opposite of a magnet. It''s an interesting composition, well exposed and focused, but without the challenge context, it seems nonsensical.</td>', 'Um, I hate to be the one to break this to you, but steel is not the opposite of a magnet. It''s an interesting composition, well exposed and focused, but without the challenge context, it seems nonsensical.', '2004-05-16 14:19:30.000000', NULL, 1),
