(725663, 75903, 17551, '<td valign="top">I think I need to explain this as many people seem have no idea what it means. Chalk &amp; Cheese is primarily a culturally based saying, meaning exact opposites. If I say "They go together like chalk &amp; cheese", It means they dont match at all. All australians would be familiar with this saying, but Americans and Europeans.. not by the sound of it :-)<br/> <br/>-Dan<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-05-19 05:14:30.</i></td>', 'I think I need to explain this as many people seem have no idea what it means. Chalk & Cheese is primarily a culturally based saying, meaning exact opposites. If I say "They go together like chalk & cheese", It means they dont match at all. All australians would be familiar with this saying, but Americans and Europeans.. not by the sound of it :-) -Dan', '2004-05-19 01:02:46.000000', '2004-05-19 06:14:30.000000', 0),
