(725675, 75921, 12268, '<td valign="top">Man! I can;t believe this didn;t ribbon. In fact I only voted so my vote of 10 for this shot would count! Great shot. By far my fave!</td>', 'Man! I can;t believe this didn;t ribbon. In fact I only voted so my vote of 10 for this shot would count! Great shot. By far my fave!', '2004-05-19 01:11:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(725677, 75854, 19608, '<td valign="top">Hi Ara and * Greetings from the Crique Club*<br/> <br/>I just critiqued your "Rust" entry a day or two ago.<br/> <br/>You will find this critique very different.<br/> <br/>When a shot is perfect and already has over 50 comments telling you so, there''s just one way:<br/> <br/><b>CONGRATULATIONS!</b></td>', 'Hi Ara and * Greetings from the Crique Club* I just critiqued your "Rust" entry a day or two ago. You will find this critique very different. When a shot is perfect and already has over 50 comments telling you so, there''s just one way: CONGRATULATIONS!', '2004-05-19 01:12:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(725687, 76026, 16106, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the kind comments,though I do wish the folks who voted one and two had left a comment too.<br/> I forgot to describe how I set up the shot so in answer to some questions here goes. I bought a large block of ice at the store, which sadly was too milky but next time Ill know, I used a blow torch to create a bowl and poured in about 3 cc of gasoline. I put the block in front of a black backdrop and on sone black paper with a square cut out which was on top of a peice of plexiglass with blue plastic on it to get the cold light, under which was a drop light in a cardboard box. I took the shots centered and cropped them slightly off to give it a less static look. I took about thirty shots over four rounds of adding gas and igniting and was pleased to have not set the garage on fire.</td>', 'Thanks for all the kind comments,though I do wish the folks who voted one and two had left a comment too. I forgot to describe how I set up the shot so in answer to some questions here goes. I bought a large block of ice at the store, which sadly was too milky but next time Ill know, I used a blow torch to create a bowl and poured in about 3 cc of gasoline. I put the block in front of a black backdrop and on sone black paper with a square cut out which was on top of a peice of plexiglass with blue plastic on it to get the cold light, under which was a drop light in a cardboard box. I took the shots centered and cropped them slightly off to give it a less static look. I took about thirty shots over four rounds of adding gas and igniting and was pleased to have not set the garage on fire.', '2004-05-19 01:19:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(725695, 76023, 6900, '<td valign="top">''grats on your first 6+.  A great image - wish the salt had a bit more detail and the one stray peppercorn needed to go. :)<br/> <br/>Mav</td>', '''grats on your first 6+.  A great image - wish the salt had a bit more detail and the one stray peppercorn needed to go. :) Mav', '2004-05-19 01:25:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(725717, 75601, 16479, '<td valign="top">I''d like to thank all of you guys for your comments, good or bad, nice or not-so-nice, it doesn''t matter....I mean all are warmly accepted. <br/> <br/>wow...a whooping 53 1''s, 50 3''s, 51 4''s and 57 5''s....<br/> <br/>I thought it is cool, I thought I''ve captured something different...yes dogs are well photograph, and the subject is rather common. But how often do you see an "action" or "scene" like this in front of your gate? <br/> <br/>This is my lowest score so far, but it really doesn''t matter to me. But who wants a lower score anyway? :( I''m pretty happy if I get an average, but will be very happy if I get a higher one. I enjoy this site very much and I love entering every challenges. I guess I should be more selective now of my entries so I won''t get slammed.<br/> <br/>Again thanks folks especially those who gave 6, 7, 8 ,9 and 10<br/> <br/>Cheers :)<br/></td>', 'I''d like to thank all of you guys for your comments, good or bad, nice or not-so-nice, it doesn''t matter....I mean all are warmly accepted.  wow...a whooping 53 1''s, 50 3''s, 51 4''s and 57 5''s.... I thought it is cool, I thought I''ve captured something different...yes dogs are well photograph, and the subject is rather common. But how often do you see an "action" or "scene" like this in front of your gate?  This is my lowest score so far, but it really doesn''t matter to me. But who wants a lower score anyway? :( I''m pretty happy if I get an average, but will be very happy if I get a higher one. I enjoy this site very much and I love entering every challenges. I guess I should be more selective now of my entries so I won''t get slammed. Again thanks folks especially those who gave 6, 7, 8 ,9 and 10 Cheers :)', '2004-05-19 01:37:27.000000', NULL, 0),
