(727928, 75921, 7810, '<td valign="top">great shot ...I liked this alot  oh yea...welcome back Jon<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-05-19 18:44:31.</i></td>', 'great shot ...I liked this alot  oh yea...welcome back Jon', '2004-05-19 19:43:56.000000', '2004-05-19 19:44:31.000000', 0),
(728071, 75644, 20679, '<td valign="top">OK - my first submission and now I know the kind of competition I am up against! I rushed this entry and shouldn''t have. Also, in retrospect I should have known that the fire/ice theme would be done to death. So 240th out of 291 is pretty dreadful, but I intend to do much better in future challenges. Thanks for the comments everyone :)</td>', 'OK - my first submission and now I know the kind of competition I am up against! I rushed this entry and shouldn''t have. Also, in retrospect I should have known that the fire/ice theme would be done to death. So 240th out of 291 is pretty dreadful, but I intend to do much better in future challenges. Thanks for the comments everyone :)', '2004-05-19 20:56:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(728347, 76009, 4494, '<td valign="top">How bizzare.  At first I thought you pasted pictures of cool little houses onto another picture, because I''ve never seen anything like this.  They look new, why would a builder build in front of that grain factory or whatever it is!  No garages but they look like nice little houses.  I bet the price is reasonable for these. :)  Nice one.</td>', 'How bizzare.  At first I thought you pasted pictures of cool little houses onto another picture, because I''ve never seen anything like this.  They look new, why would a builder build in front of that grain factory or whatever it is!  No garages but they look like nice little houses.  I bet the price is reasonable for these. :)  Nice one.', '2004-05-20 00:13:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(728405, 76073, 15768, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bigjohnny:</b></div><hr/><i> hehehehe i knew it was you! with the red and the blue, of course its aleks! hehehe </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ya... thanks for the colored gels. I''m making great use of them. And I''m taking good care of your lights. Enjoy Europe!</td>', 'Originally posted by bigjohnny: hehehehe i knew it was you! with the red and the blue, of course its aleks! hehehe   Ya... thanks for the colored gels. I''m making great use of them. And I''m taking good care of your lights. Enjoy Europe!', '2004-05-20 00:44:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(728435, 76032, 16269, '<td valign="top">I voted - and commented - on this photograph already, but I wanted to come back to it. This was one of my favorite photos, though I was pretty sure you were going to get some of the comments like "does not fit the challenge." Phooey, I say! I think the focus on the flower and blur of the weeds only adds MORE opposition. Now we have flower/weeds AND focused/unfocused. And anyway, people really do tend to dote on the flower more than the weed. It really shows peoples views on each element: they adore the flower and ignore the weeds. Anyway. I love it. I think that the "rule of thirds" would ruin this shot. Gorgeous gorgeous work.. blows mine out of the water.<br/> <br/>Those are my two cents, anyway (or was it two dollars by now? I''ll stop rambling.)</td>', 'I voted - and commented - on this photograph already, but I wanted to come back to it. This was one of my favorite photos, though I was pretty sure you were going to get some of the comments like "does not fit the challenge." Phooey, I say! I think the focus on the flower and blur of the weeds only adds MORE opposition. Now we have flower/weeds AND focused/unfocused. And anyway, people really do tend to dote on the flower more than the weed. It really shows peoples views on each element: they adore the flower and ignore the weeds. Anyway. I love it. I think that the "rule of thirds" would ruin this shot. Gorgeous gorgeous work.. blows mine out of the water. Those are my two cents, anyway (or was it two dollars by now? I''ll stop rambling.)', '2004-05-20 01:05:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(728470, 75854, 8911, '<td valign="top">This is a great shot, and gorgeous. And I agree with earlier comments - don''t be too modest about this! It is a lot knowing where to point your camera and when, and being willing to take the time and focus to do so. It sure sounds like this storm made the photography a lot easier than a milder storm would, but that doesn''t make this photo any less impressive or any less to your credit, IMO. Right place, right time - still only matters if you have what''s needed to take advantage of it!</td>', 'This is a great shot, and gorgeous. And I agree with earlier comments - don''t be too modest about this! It is a lot knowing where to point your camera and when, and being willing to take the time and focus to do so. It sure sounds like this storm made the photography a lot easier than a milder storm would, but that doesn''t make this photo any less impressive or any less to your credit, IMO. Right place, right time - still only matters if you have what''s needed to take advantage of it!', '2004-05-20 01:31:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(728472, 75281, 11432, '<td valign="top">I like the use of color, the Red vs Blue, is just like the Hot vs Cold. Good choices. Your lighting of the pepper is good, I would have liked to see a pepper that was a different color, I don''t know. I do like the way that the Ice interacts with the background and the tissue paper it is sitting on. <br/>As this is your second entry you are doing good, you are getting a better score on your shots and I hope to see more shots.</td>', 'I like the use of color, the Red vs Blue, is just like the Hot vs Cold. Good choices. Your lighting of the pepper is good, I would have liked to see a pepper that was a different color, I don''t know. I do like the way that the Ice interacts with the background and the tissue paper it is sitting on. As this is your second entry you are doing good, you are getting a better score on your shots and I hope to see more shots.', '2004-05-20 01:33:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(728501, 75969, 16487, '<td valign="top">Nice job!!</td>', 'Nice job!!', '2004-05-20 02:20:21.000000', NULL, 0),
