(736052, 75321, 4493, '<td valign="top">Critique Club:<br/> <br/>Howdee and congrats!<br/> <br/>Overall I think this is a fine image. The contrasting subjects work very well. I do however have reservations with how tight the subjects are to the center line. I think that giving ample room in the middle and then working to get your exposure just right in the camera so as to minimize the NI, you''d have a museum quality shot. <br/> <br/>Thank you for the original shot!<br/>-danny</td>', 'Critique Club: Howdee and congrats! Overall I think this is a fine image. The contrasting subjects work very well. I do however have reservations with how tight the subjects are to the center line. I think that giving ample room in the middle and then working to get your exposure just right in the camera so as to minimize the NI, you''d have a museum quality shot.  Thank you for the original shot!-danny', '2004-05-25 22:40:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(742410, 75992, 20395, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critque Club!<br/> <br/>This picture is very hard for me to critique from a non-emotional level, which is good. It means that your photo is strong enough to cause a reaction in a viewer. Personally, it pulls at both my concern for the current military action in Iraq and my friend the Marine who will be beginning his second tour of duty in Iraq soon. It highlights for me that soldiers cannot be lumped up with the government as one big entity- that they are both citizens and soldiers, a strong opposite indeed sometimes. <br/> <br/>Compositionally, I have some problems with it. I''d rather there be one photo than two, as it splits the focus, and the photo you chose to highlight is a little wonky. The arch in the picture is confusing- because the hat butts up against it the arch looks like a cuttout or frame instead of part of the picture. Instead of a second photo, some objects of home life might have worked better against the uniform. I do like the slight desaturation very much. <br/> <br/>I hope this is helpful, please feel free to email me and questions or comments!<br/>Amanda</td>', 'Greetings from the Critque Club! This picture is very hard for me to critique from a non-emotional level, which is good. It means that your photo is strong enough to cause a reaction in a viewer. Personally, it pulls at both my concern for the current military action in Iraq and my friend the Marine who will be beginning his second tour of duty in Iraq soon. It highlights for me that soldiers cannot be lumped up with the government as one big entity- that they are both citizens and soldiers, a strong opposite indeed sometimes.  Compositionally, I have some problems with it. I''d rather there be one photo than two, as it splits the focus, and the photo you chose to highlight is a little wonky. The arch in the picture is confusing- because the hat butts up against it the arch looks like a cuttout or frame instead of part of the picture. Instead of a second photo, some objects of home life might have worked better against the uniform. I do like the slight desaturation very much.  I hope this is helpful, please feel free to email me and questions or comments!Amanda', '2004-05-30 10:44:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(742553, 74721, 18202, '<td valign="top">That''s much better mate!<br/>Sorry for the harsh comment before, I''m glad it helped though :)<br/>Now it looks way better..Though now the opposites are less obvious.<br/>Keep trying, you''re getting better :)</td>', 'That''s much better mate!Sorry for the harsh comment before, I''m glad it helped though :)Now it looks way better..Though now the opposites are less obvious.Keep trying, you''re getting better :)', '2004-05-30 14:19:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(747368, 75909, 7322, '<td valign="top">I liked this photo quite a bit and if I had been using my current voting methods for this challenge (didn''t know I could revise votes for one thing) I probably would have scored it higher than the 6 I gave it. <br/> <br/>I caught the opposite right away. The title helps without nailing the viewer over the head (although judging by some of the comments, it seems some people need to be slapped in the face with an idea before they get it). <br/> <br/>I like the slight over exposure on the faces. I think it heightens the slight skewing of reality for the viewer. The tilted format achieves this as well. I don''t know if you intended this but that''s how it works for me.<br/> I like how their black clothes disappear into the background. The models are beautiful.</td>', 'I liked this photo quite a bit and if I had been using my current voting methods for this challenge (didn''t know I could revise votes for one thing) I probably would have scored it higher than the 6 I gave it.  I caught the opposite right away. The title helps without nailing the viewer over the head (although judging by some of the comments, it seems some people need to be slapped in the face with an idea before they get it).  I like the slight over exposure on the faces. I think it heightens the slight skewing of reality for the viewer. The tilted format achieves this as well. I don''t know if you intended this but that''s how it works for me. I like how their black clothes disappear into the background. The models are beautiful.', '2004-06-02 15:16:45.000000', NULL, 0),
