(2623102, 76031, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by meanwile:</b></div><hr/><i> I like the idea.  I guess the ''artwork'' rules were different at this time? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>No, those are real hands in front of the monitor -- legal under Basic rules today too. That''s one thing which made it difficult to shoot; I had to both operate the camera (no remote) and get in position to "model" for the hands where they and the monitor would have the proper size and DOF relationship.</td>', 'Originally posted by meanwile: I like the idea.  I guess the ''artwork'' rules were different at this time?  No, those are real hands in front of the monitor -- legal under Basic rules today too. That''s one thing which made it difficult to shoot; I had to both operate the camera (no remote) and get in position to "model" for the hands where they and the monitor would have the proper size and DOF relationship.', '2006-07-14 19:32:21.000000', NULL, 0),
